# MuPRO settings for the STK Runtime; workers inherit them (docs/runtime-mupro.md).
# Copy to ~/.config/stk/mupro.env, chmod 600, then enable EnvironmentFile in
# stk-supervisor.service and restart it after every change; running workers keep
# their old environment. Paths only: STK never reads, prints or copies licence files.
MUPRO_SDK_PREFIX=/opt/mupro/sdk
# Licence directory, at most 256 bytes.
MUPROROOT=/path/to/licence-dir
# Bash scripts sourced before each launch, separated by ':'.
STK_MUPRO_ENV_SCRIPTS=/opt/intel/oneapi/mpi/latest/env/vars.sh:/path/to/compiler-runtime.sh
# Allows mpiexec outside a Slurm/PBS allocation. Intel MPI's Hydra then listens on
# 0.0.0.0 while the job runs; set it only on a host other networks cannot reach.
# Tasks cannot set it in their env, but this guards against accidental local runs
# only: Runtime clients can run any command, so the token, loopback binding and the
# host firewall are the access controls.
# STK_MUPRO_ALLOW_LOCAL_MPI=1
